\newpage
\begin{verbatim}
%
% RULE RbyEMPTYsubst
< m1: I1::CLAUSE{CLAUSErec1}
                [ mu1,
                  predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}
                         [ I2:mu2,
                           byobjrel/VARPREPP{VARPREPPrec1}
                                   [ head/PREP(KEY_doorbyprepkey){PREPrec1},
                                     objrel/I3::EMPTYVAR{EMPTYVARrec1}
                                   ]
                         ],
                   mu3
                 ]

  SUBST:
  m2: EMPTY(KEY_oneEMPTYkey){EMPTYrec1} 
>

< m : I1::CLAUSE{CLAUSErec1}
                [ mu1,
                  predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}[I2:mu2],
                  mu3
                ]
>

   MATCHCONDITIONS
      <
       I1: CLAUSErec1.voice = passive
       I2: NOT EXIST (mu2, [byobjrel/..])
       I3: EMPTYVARrec1.index = LEVEL
      >

   PARAMETERS
      <
       LEVEL
      >

      COMP
         <
          C1: EMPTYVARrec1 = { person : 3
                               number : singular
                               gender : omegagender }
              (* same as oneEMPTY *) AND
              VARPREPPrec1 = PREPPrecdef 
                EXCEPT FOR [actsubcefs, synppefs, thetapp, headkey,
                            mood, specQ] 
              AND
              VARPREPPrec1 = { actsubcefs : [doorby]
                               synppefs   : [synEMPTY]
                               thetapp    : pp120
                               mood       : nowh
                               specQ      : yesspec
                               headkey    : KEY_doorbyprepkey }
          A1: @
         >
      DECOMP
         <
          C1: true
          A1: VARPREPPrec1 := { actsubcefs : [doorby]
                                synppefs   : [synEMPTY]
                                thetapp    : pp120
                                mood       : nowh
                                specQ      : yesspec
                                headkey    : KEY_doorbyprepkey }
              (* other attributes keep default values *);
              EMPTYVARrec1 := { index  : LEVEL
                                person : 3
                                number : singular
                                gender : omegagender }
         >
&

\end{verbatim}
\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* name:] RbyEMPTYsubst
\item[* relevant examples:] (VERBPPROP example:) [I had] built a house by EMPTY 
$\rightarrow$ [I had] built a house\\
-- was built the house in 1918 by EMPTY $\rightarrow$ -- was built the house in 
1918
\item[* language:] (Dutch, English, Spanish) English
\item[* kind of rule:] (M-rule, S-rule, Transferrule) M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] XPPROPtoCLAUSE
\item[* class:] (name of rule, transformation or filter class) 
RC\_EMPTYsubstitution
\item[* date of creation:] 11-MAR-1988 14:26:43  
\item[* author:] margreet sanders
\item[* copied from:] --
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] delete a byobj when there is an EMPTY as substituent (in 
generation)
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals)
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:]
\item[\ \ clarification of variables:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the splitting up into subrules:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the collapsing of rules:] (e.g. clarification of parameters)
\item[\ \ differences analytical/generative version:]
\item[\  \ suggested semantics:]
\item[\ \ presuppositions:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item dictionary:\\

\item rules:\\
It is assumed that the oneEMPTYkey is the best choice here. Correctness of this 
choice can be checked when there is a reflexive: {\em It was decided (by 
oneEMPTY) to behave oneself\/}; although other reflexives also seem possible.
Note that the 
attribute values of the EMPTY will probably only matter for NOC.\\
It is assumed that the byobjrel/.. is always the rightmost element of the VERBP
. Given the (analytic) conditions on the order of application of the other
EMPTYsubst 
rules, this rule will have to apply last in analysis. In generation, the 
substitution order is determined by what order occurred in the source language.
\end{enumerate}
\item[\ \ consequences in the grammar:]
\item[\ \ translation aspects:]\mbox{}
