\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* name:] RprepEMPTYsubst2
\item[* relevant examples:] \mbox{}\\
\begin{enumerate}
\item synPREPNP\_EMPTY:\\
(vp123): x1 talked to x3 EMPTY $\rightarrow$ x1 talked to x3\\
To prevent all structures containing a prepobj from being covered by this rule, 
the second prepobj is explicitly mentioned in the left model. In analysis, one 
wrong path is created: the case where the synpattern is synEMPTY\_PREPNP 
i.s.o.\ synPREPNP\_EMPTY. This 
path will be filtered out only in the startrules, where the prep going with the 
direct object is in wrong position (it should be second, instead of first).
Remember that in the pattern rules 
only one canonical argument order is allowed: x1 talk to x3 about x2 , i.e.\ 
first the goal (`indirect object'), then the theme (`direct object').
\end{enumerate}
\item[* language:] (Dutch, English, Spanish) English
\item[* kind of rule:] (M-rule, S-rule, Transferrule) M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] XPPROPtoCLAUSE
\item[* class:] (name of rule, transformation or filter class) 
RC\_EMPTYsubstitution
\item[* date of creation:] 23-MAR-1988 
\item[* author:] margreet sanders
\item[* copied from:] RprepEMPTYsubst1
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] delete the second prepobj when there is an EMPTY as substituent 
(in generation)
