\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* name:] ROneSubjEMPTYsubst
\item[* relevant examples:] One can never tell (can one?)
\item[* language:] (Dutch, English, Spanish) English
\item[* kind of rule:] (M-rule, S-rule, Transferrule) M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] XPPROPtoCLAUSE
\item[* class:] (name of rule, transformation or filter class)
RC\_EMPTYsubstitution
\item[* date of creation:] 11-MAR-1988 15:47:59  
\item[* author:] margreet sanders
\item[* copied from:]
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: 13/10/89\ \ \ \ \ author: Lisette Appelo\\
Deleted decomp part: {\em one\/} is considered a basic expression now, and 
translates into the basic expression {\em men\/}. The rule is needed only for 
those cases where there was an empty in the source language, e.g.\  {\em Er 
werd gedanst\/} - {\em One danced\/}.
\item date: 9/11/89\ \ \ \ \ author: Margreet Sanders\\
Removed condition on finiteness of clause, to allow for the translation {\em 
He let one hear the music\/} for the Dutch {\em Hij liet de muziek (aan EMPTY) 
horen\/}. If this is considered incorrect, there still is another path for 
transitive verbs: passivisation: {\em he let the music be heard (by EMPTY)\/}
(see RPassive1).
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] insert a subject where there was an EMPTYVAR
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals) It is assumed 
that Dutch {\em men\/} will be mapped onto English {\em one\/} and vv, but also 
Dutch {\em je\/}. There seem to be restrictions on the use of {\em one\/} as 
translation of {\em je\/}, but these have not been formulated yet. Therefore, 
no rule for English YouSubj/ObjEMPTYsubst exists yet.\\
9/11/89: the rule that spells out an empty subject as {\em They\/} has been 
removed, since it no longer seems needed (see above, RTheySubjEMPTYsubst).
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:]
\item[\ \ clarification of variables:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the splitting up into subrules:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the collapsing of rules:] (e.g. clarification of parameters)
\item[\ \ differences analytical/generative version:] 
