\newpage
\begin{verbatim}
% RULE REMPTYinADJPsubst
< m1: I1::CLAUSE{CLAUSErec1}
                [ mu1,
                  predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}
                         [ mu2,
                           predrel/ADJP{ADJPrec1}
                                  [ mu9,
                                    head/ADJ{ADJrec1}[mu10],
                                    mu5
                                  ],
                           mu3
                         ],
                  mu4
                ]
  SUBST:
  m2: EMPTY(KEY_zeroEMPTYkey){EMPTYrec1}
>

< m : I2::CLAUSE{CLAUSErec2}
                [ mu1,
                  predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}
                         [ mu2,
                           predrel/ADJP{ADJPrec2}
                                  [ mu9,
                                    head/ADJ{ADJrec1}[mu10],
                                    mu6
                                  ],
                           mu3
                         ],
                  mu4
                ]
>

   MATCHCONDITIONS
      <
       I1: synBE IN CLAUSErec1.synvpefs
       I2: synBE IN CLAUSErec2.synvpefs
      >

   PARAMETERS
      <
       LEVEL
      >

<
   SUBRULE (* 1. prepobj *)
      < mu5: [ I7:mu7,
               prepobjrel/I3::EMPTYVAR{EMPTYVARrec1},
               I8:mu8
             ] >
      < mu6: [ I7:mu7, I9:mu8 ] >

   MATCHCONDITIONS
      <
       I3: EMPTYVARrec1.index = LEVEL
       I7: ALL (mu7, I71:rel1/..)
       I8: NOT EXIST (mu8, [I71:rel1/..]) AND 
           NOT EXIST (mu8, [prepobjrel/..])
       I9: NOT EXIST (mu8, [I71:rel1/..]) AND 
           NOT EXIST (mu8, [prepobjrel/..]) AND
           NOT EXIST (mu8, [../EMPTYVAR{}]) AND
           NOT EXIST (mu8, [../VARPREPP{}[I91:mu11]]) 
       (* the last two conditions are for substorder *)
         I71: rel1 IN [ objrel, complrel, locargrel, dirargrel,
                        forobjrel ]
         I91: EXIST (mu11, [../EMPTYVAR{}])
      >

      COMP
         <
          C1: ADJPrec1.adjpatternefs * [synPREPEMPTY] <> [] AND
              EMPTYVARrec1 = { person : 3
                               number : omeganumber
                               gender : omegagender }
          A1: CLAUSErec2 := CLAUSErec1;
              CLAUSErec2.synvpefs := CLAUSErec1.synvpefs * [synBE];
              ADJPrec2 := ADJPrec1;
              ADJPrec2.adjpatternefs := 
                     ADJPrec1.adjpatternefs * [synPREPEMPTY]
         >
      DECOMP
         <
          C1: ADJPrec2.adjpatternefs * [synPREPEMPTY] <> [] 
          A1: EMPTYVARrec1 := { person : 3
                                number : omeganumber
                                gender : omegagender 
                                index  : LEVEL };
              CLAUSErec1 := CLAUSErec2;
              CLAUSErec1.synvpefs := CLAUSErec2.synvpefs * [synBE];
              ADJPrec1 := ADJPrec2;
              ADJPrec1.adjpatternefs := 
                     ADJPrec2.adjpatternefs * [synPREPEMPTY]
         >

   SUBRULE (* 2. locargrel *)
      < mu5: [ I7:mu7,
               locargrel/I3::EMPTYVAR{EMPTYVARrec1},
               I8:mu8
             ] >
      < mu6: [ I7:mu7, I9:mu8 ] >

   MATCHCONDITIONS
      <
       I3: EMPTYVARrec1.index = LEVEL
       I7: ALL (mu7, I71:rel1/..)
       I8: NOT EXIST (mu8, [I71:rel1/..]) AND 
           NOT EXIST (mu8, [locargrel/..])
       I9: NOT EXIST (mu8, [I71:rel1/..]) AND 
           NOT EXIST (mu8, [locargrel/..]) AND
           NOT EXIST (mu8, [../EMPTYVAR{}]) AND
           NOT EXIST (mu8, [../VARPREPP{}[I91:mu11]]) 
       (* the last two conditions are for substorder *)
         I71: rel1 IN [ objrel, complrel ]
         I91: EXIST (mu11, [../EMPTYVAR{}])
      >

      COMP
         <
          C1: ADJPrec1.adjpatternefs * [synLOCEMPTY] <> [] AND
              EMPTYVARrec1 = { person : 3
                               number : omeganumber
                               gender : omegagender }
          A1: CLAUSErec2 := CLAUSErec1;
              CLAUSErec2.synvpefs := CLAUSErec1.synvpefs * [synBE];
              ADJPrec2 := ADJPrec1;
              ADJPrec2.adjpatternefs := 
                     ADJPrec1.adjpatternefs * [synLOCEMPTY]
         >
      DECOMP
         <
          C1: ADJPrec2.adjpatternefs * [synLOCEMPTY] <> [] 
          A1: EMPTYVARrec1 := { person : 3
                                number : omeganumber
                                gender : omegagender 
                                index  : LEVEL };
              CLAUSErec1 := CLAUSErec2;
              CLAUSErec1.synvpefs := CLAUSErec2.synvpefs * [synBE];
              ADJPrec1 := ADJPrec2;
              ADJPrec1.adjpatternefs := 
                     ADJPrec2.adjpatternefs * [synLOCEMPTY]
         >
>

&

\end{verbatim}
\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* name:] REMPTYinADJPsubst
\item[* relevant examples:] \mbox{}\\
subrule 1: he was afraid (of) EMPTY\\
subrule 2: I am settled down (in) EMPTY
\item[* language:] (Dutch, English, Spanish) English
\item[* kind of rule:] (M-rule, S-rule, Transferrule) M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] XPPROPtoCLAUSE
\item[* class:] (name of rule, transformation or filter class) RC\_
EMPTYsubstitution
\item[* date of creation:] 6-APR-1989 15:15:33  
\item[* author:] margreet sanders
\item[* copied from:] Dutch Rsadjemptysubst (but adapted)
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] to substitute for empty arguments occurring under a predrel/ADJP
and delete them; all this only in case the ADJP is not part of an OPEN/CLOSED
ADJPPROP (
then, the substitution should take place in the ADJPPROP subgrammar).
\item[\ \ strategy:] (also: deviations from accepted proposals) Note that the 
adjpatternefs of the ADJP and the synpatternefs of the CLAUSE are reduced to the 
only possibility; thus, during analysis it will be discovered in the pattern 
rules whether substitution was correct, i.e. whether this sentence indeed was 
not derived from a full ADJPPROP.
\item[\ \ rejected alternatives:]
\item[\ \ clarification of variables:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the splitting up into subrules:]
\item[\ \ clarification of the collapsing of rules:] (e.g. clarification of parameters)
\item[\ \ differences analytical/generative version:] In analysis, a condition 
has been formulated on the order of EMPTYsubst-rule application: the leftmost 
EMPTYVAR must be introduced first. This prevents many (correct) ambiguities, 
caused only by a different order of application of the substitution rules. Now, 
all orders of application leaving some EMPTYVARs unintroduced will be filtered 
out later (probably only in the pattern rules, where the number of arguments is 
counted) as incorrect.\\
In generation, the order of substitution is determined by the order found in 
the source language.
\item[\  \ suggested semantics:]
\item[\ \ presuppositions:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item dictionary:\\

\item rules:\\
It is assumed that English does not need a rule for substitution of indobj/
EMPTYVARs (there is no adjpatternrule for that either). Perhaps, rules will be 
needed for toobj (or forobj) EMPTYs, but these pattern rules have not been 
formulated yet. The exact ordering of relations in the ADJP is not clear to me;
the formulation chosen here may be wrong (Franciska has not defined an `
AdjRelPrec').
\end{enumerate}
\item[\ \ consequences in the grammar:]
\item[\ \ translation aspects:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate} 
\item within this language:\\

\item in other languages:\\

\end{enumerate}
\item[* relevant literature/documents:]
